{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\froman\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1\fswiss\fcharset0 Arial;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue128;}{\info{\title Sample RTF Document}{\author Jane Doe}{\subject RTF Viewer Demo}{\keywords rtf sample demo text}{\doccomm This document demonstrates RTF text extraction in the file viewer.}}{\*\generator RTF Sample Generator 1.0;}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs24 {\b Sample RTF Document}\par \par This is a sample {\b Rich Text Format} document created to demonstrate the RTF text extraction capability of the file viewer. RTF is an older Microsoft format that supports {\i rich formatting} such as bold and italic text, font changes, and more.\par \par {\b About RTF Parsing}\par \par The viewer extracts plain text from RTF files, stripping all formatting control words. Special characters are handled via Windows-1252 encoding, so caf\'e9 and r\'e9sum\'e9 appear correctly. Unicode escapes also work: the word \u233?clair demonstrates the \\u escape mechanism.\par \par {\b International Text}\par \par RTF supports multilingual content. Here are some examples using hex escapes: na\'efve, fa\'e7ade, d\'e9j\'e0 vu, and caf\'e9. The Windows-1252 code page covers most Western European characters.\par \par {\b A Longer Passage}\par \par Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.\par \par This document was authored by {\b Jane Doe} and serves as a test fixture for the RTF plugin in the file-viewer project.\par}
